course: dictionary
lesson: 10458
title: Truthfulness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Truthfulness means being honest and always telling the truth. It is a noun, and it can also mean how true or accurate something is: people check the truthfulness of a story before they believe it.
explain: In Kenneth Grahame's story, the Rat says, «There, what did I tell you?» The Mole answers «Absolutely nothing whatever», and he says it with perfect truthfulness. The Rat had really not told him anything, so the Mole was being honest, even though his answer is a bit funny.
explain: Truthfulness is close to honesty and sincerity, but it is about telling the truth in what you say. Stories about heroes often show it, because they tell the truth even when it is hard. Look for clues like "even when it is hard" to see when a writer is praising truthfulness.
explain: Nearly everyone agrees that honesty should be the rule, with exceptions rare and serious. In one text, a vicar says, "Honour your parents, yet our first obedience is to God, who asks truthfulness of us." The writer treats truthfulness as very important, so the words around it tell you what is valued.
fact: Truthfulness means being honest and always telling the truth.
fact: Truthfulness can also mean how true or accurate something is, as in «the truthfulness of the story».
fact: Truthfulness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some truthfulness, not a truthfulness.
fact: Honesty and sincerity are close synonyms, but truthfulness focuses on telling the truth.
fact: Not everything online is true, so check facts and rumours before you believe them.
exercise: What does truthfulness mean? | Being happy in a crowd | Being very fast at running | Keeping secrets from everyone | *Being honest and always telling the truth
exercise: The Mole answers «Absolutely nothing whatever» with perfect truthfulness. What does this show? | He is asking a question | *He is being honest, and the Rat really had told him nothing | He is lying to save the Rat's feelings | He has not heard the Rat speak
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to truthfulness? | Rudeness | Sadness | Speed | *Honesty
test: In the sentence «They checked the truthfulness of the story», what is being checked? | The story's pictures | The name of the author | *Whether the story is true and accurate | The length of the story
test: Which is a good example of truthfulness? | *Telling your teacher the truth about the broken window | Pretending you were never near the window | Hiding a broken window under the mat | Blaming your little brother for the broken window
exam: Jayden says truthfulness just means being quiet. Is he right? | Yes, quiet people are always truthful | *No, truthfulness is about telling the truth, not about staying quiet | Only in libraries | Only on Tuesdays
